select, combobox: Track choices by value

Row indices are positions in the filtered or paged list, not items. A search
or page response can replace a row between Enter and the deferred confirm.

- The searchable list confirms the item itself. Select's deferred confirm,
  cancel and query reset find the item by value again.
- Combobox compares selected values, not rows, before and after
  on_will_change. Replacing A at row 0 with filtered B at row 0 now emits
  Change and Confirm; moving the same value to another row does not.
- ComboboxEvent::Activate reports an accepted activation, separately from
  Confirm, which also fires on dismissal. Activating the current item closes
  a single-select combobox without a false Change.
- ComboboxState::close dismisses without focus changes or selection events.
- Select::is_open, Select::menu_scroll_handle and
  Select::menu_item_min_height (a minimum row height independent of the
  trigger size).
- List rows report to test-support snapshots, so tests can measure menu
  rows.

Remove when upstream confirms by value and offers these hooks.

